annotation.description:
Excludes the following constant or enum from de-const/de-enum export processing, preserving its declaration and metadata. This annotation also applies to local constants.
[codeblock]
@no_mangle
const API_ENDPOINT = "https://example.com"

func example() -> void:
	@no_mangle
	const DEBUG_LABEL = "debug"
[/codeblock]

Marks the following script, class, or function as excluded from export-time string obfuscation.
Hardcoded [code]String[/code], [code]StringName[/code], and [code]NodePath[/code] literals inside the annotated scope are not encoded as resource-backed markers. Other export transforms still apply. If a constant string is removed by de-const and inlined at a usage site, the usage site's scope controls whether the inlined string is obfuscated.
[codeblock]
@no_string_mangle
class_name ScriptWithVisibleStrings

@no_string_mangle
func print_user_message() -> void:
	print("This string is not string-obfuscated on export.")
[/codeblock]

Marks a script or class as participating in wgodot partial-script declarations. The optional [param path] argument can identify the source fragment or companion script path used by tooling.
This annotation is currently recognized by the parser so projects and tools can use the marker without producing an unknown annotation error.
[codeblock]
@partial
class_name PlayerController

@partial("res://player/player_controller_input.gd")
class InputPart:
	pass
[/codeblock]

Marks the following class-level member as private to the current class.
Private members cannot be accessed from outside the class that declares them. This annotation can be used on nested classes, constants, functions, signals, and variables, and cannot be combined with [annotation @protected].
[codeblock]
@private
var inventory_cache: Dictionary[String, int]

@private
func rebuild_cache() -> void:
	pass
[/codeblock]

Marks the following class-level member as protected.
Protected members can be accessed from the class that declares them and from inherited classes, but not from unrelated classes. This annotation can be used on nested classes, constants, functions, signals, and variables, and cannot be combined with [annotation @private].
[codeblock]
@protected
var health: int

@protected
func apply_damage(amount: int) -> void:
	pass
[/codeblock]

Marks the following variable as assignable only during initialization.
Local variables marked [annotation @readonly] must be assigned where they are declared. Class fields marked [annotation @readonly] can be assigned where they are declared or inside the class initializer, but cannot be reassigned later.
[codeblock]
@readonly
var id := 0

func example() -> void:
	@readonly
	var label := "ready"
[/codeblock]
